{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-19_13-32-32-dragonboat_raft-real-run/state.json'))\nfor e in s.get('executions',[]):\n    if e['id'] in ('df751474c61249939d500ad57df6586c','128e306bc45e4348953c46c22c75f484'):\n        print(e['id'], e['status'], e['test_selection']['requested'])\n        for i,ev in enumerate(e['events']):\n            print(' ', i, ev.get('event'), {k:v for k,v in ev.items() if not k.startswith('_')})\nit=[i for i in s['interpretations'] if i['id']=='d55b40f35fac477a8275442974187ab9-interpretation-0'][0]\nprint(json.dumps({k:it[k] for k in ('source_ids','executions','conclusion','defect_claim','counterevidence','limitations','rationale')},indent=1))\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"node_notify_config_change\",\n  \"node_get_cluster_info\",\n  \"nodehost_cluster_info_type\",\n  \"nodehost_get_nodehost_info\",\n  \"nodehost_cluster_info_list\",\n  \"nodehost_sync_get_cluster_membership\"\n ],\n \"executions\": {\n  \"df751474c61249939d500ad57df6586c\": [\n   0,\n   1,\n   2\n  ],\n  \"128e306bc45e4348953c46c22c75f484\": [\n   1,\n   2\n  ]\n },\n \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"NodeHost.SyncGetClusterMembership returns the public Membership type with a Witnesses map, so callers that consult membership rather than the summary can still identify which nodes are witnesses.\",\n  \"No captured consumer reads ClusterInfo.IsWitness, and internal witness enforcement uses config.IsWitness and the raft membership, so the misreported field changes no decision, request result or stored data.\",\n  \"The pending branch fills its other fields correctly (cluster ID, node ID, state machine type, pending flag), so the observation is not evidence of a generally broken rebuild.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"NodeHost.GetNodeHostInfo is not invoked end to end; the path from it through NodeHost.getClusterInfo to node.getClusterInfo is traced in source only, and no live witness NodeHost cluster participates, because the captured witness harness needs a TCP listener that the supplied isolation denies.\",\n  \"Both receipts are object-level: the node has no raft peer, so the leader flag is false by construction and says nothing about leadership reporting.\",\n  \"The membership in the newer receipt was built from two configuration-change entries; longer membership histories, and the participant-side effects of the same changes, are not part of this account.\",\n  \"One execution of each harness and one schedule; the function under test is a pure rebuild of stored state, so repetition is not expected to change the observation.\"\n ],\n \"rationale\": \"Current claim: the per-cluster summary returned to a client never identifies a witness node as a witness, and the omission is specific to that flag rather than to the rebuild as a whole. The retained receipt df751474c61249939d500ad57df6586c executed TestAssuranceClusterInfoWitnessFlag and passed with three parsed events. Event 0 'witness_record' stored a record with IsWitness true on a node whose config.IsWitness is also true and recorded reported_is_witness=false while config_index 7, node_count 3 and pending=false came through unchanged. Event 1 'observer_record' came from an otherwise identical stored record with IsObserver true and recorded reported_is_observer=true, so the rebuild does carry the other role flag. Event 2 'pending_record' on a witness-configured node with no stored record recorded pending=true and reported_is_witness=false. A second retained receipt, 128e306bc45e4348953c46c22c75f484, produces the stored record through the target's own code rather than supplying it: its event 1 records is_witness=true in the record written by node.notifyConfigChange after the state machine applied an AddNode entry and an AddWitness entry for the local node, and its event 2 records is_witness=false in the value node.getClusterInfo returned for that same node, with identical config_index 2 and node_count 1 in both. The source accounts for exactly this pattern: node.notifyConfigChange derives both flags from the membership's Observers and Witnesses maps and stores them (node.go:1496-1518), while node.getClusterInfo copies ClusterID, NodeID, IsObserver, ConfigChangeIndex and Nodes, recomputes IsLeader and StateMachineType, and assigns no IsWitness (node.go:1520-1540). node.getClusterInfo is the only producer of NodeHostInfo.ClusterInfoList (nodehost.go:1835-1847), which NodeHost.GetNodeHostInfo returns to callers (nodehost.go:1418-1437), and no other code writes ClusterInfo.IsWitness. The field is documented as indicating whether this is a witness node without actual log (nodehost.go:163-188), so for a witness node the returned value contradicts the documented meaning of the field it fills: a management caller enumerating clusters through GetNodeHostInfo cannot tell a witness from a full voting member. Scope of the defect: it is a reporting defect on a public client contract, not a consensus defect. Witness behaviour itself is decided from config.IsWitness and from the raft and membership witness sets, so proposal, read and config-change rejection on a witness, quorum accounting and commit decisions are unaffected, and nothing in the captured tree consumes ClusterInfo.IsWitness. The harm is confined to callers that rely on the summary field: tooling that enumerates ClusterInfoList to count data-bearing replicas would count a witness as a data copy, which matters because the captured witness contract states that a witness replicates no entries and holds no state machine. The information is not lost from the API, since NodeHost.SyncGetClusterMembership returns a Membership whose Witnesses map names the witnesses (nodehost.go:633-668), so a caller consulting membership can still identify the witness role.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
