{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Traced the durability ordering behind a granted vote, the one node decision whose loss to a crash could allow a second vote in the same term, and recorded it as a new investigation (@vote_durability_before_response) with a Behavior and a source-grounded, defect-refuting account. The vote handler only sets the raft vote field and appends a response to the message buffer; the engine writes the raft state of the whole update batch before calling the step that sends every non-free-order message, and only replicate and ping bypass that write; the written state is term, vote and commit, committed with the entries in one logdb batch, and a restart reloads it through the state-loading gate. Limits kept explicit: source-only (no crash executed), the logdb's own fsync contract and its state-cache short-circuit are preconditions rather than traced behaviour, and transport queuing plus joint/witness vote paths are outside the trace. I also checked whether the asserted witness-reporting defect could be strengthened by the captured API documentation and found that account already cites the field's documented meaning, so it was left unchanged.\"}"}}
